{"aggregate_id": "01KZ23TA6Z7T25C1KVXWMWJ825", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01KZ23TAAM8ZFP616NXKHFAPMG", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"created_at": "2026-08-02T20:49:30.336989+00:00", "friendly_name": "The waiter listens instead of polling", "mission_id": "01KZ23TA6Z7T25C1KVXWMWJ825", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "wake-without-polling-01KZ23TA", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Two halves of push already exist and do not touch. The asyncRewake Stop hook can wake an idle Claude Code session, but reaches that decision by polling check_inbox every five seconds for up to eight hours \u2014 5,760 requests per wait, and up to five seconds of latency on mail that the hub knew about instantly. Meanwhile the hub emits server-sent events per actor and the MCP server already holds that stream, using it for a decision layer whose every allowed outcome currently ends 'no-adapter' because nothing can interrupt a running turn. This mission joins them: the waiter subscribes to the same stream, with polling kept as the portable floor for any hub or network that cannot hold one. It does not attempt mid-turn interruption, which needs a harness capability Claude Code does not expose.", "purpose_tldr": "An idle session wakes the moment mail arrives, because the waiter holds the hub's event stream instead of asking it every five seconds.", "target_branch": "main", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "agent-mail", "project_uuid": "d4029717-cdee-49ee-a034-fea8e7368926", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-08-02T20:49:30.452797+00:00"}
